  "alt": "Beta reduction at three levels of difficulty. A direct application reaches its normal form in one substitution. A chained application takes more than one step, keeping its bindings, before it reaches a normal form. The Omega combinator reduces to itself forever, so the correct answer is to detect that it has no normal form rather than invent a terminating one.",
  "caption": "The third tier separates a system that notices Ω never finishes from one that writes a tidy answer for it.",
